## 🏗️ Project Architecture

### Overview
This project bridges Claude Desktop with Foundry VTT for Warhammer Fantasy Roleplay 4th Edition. It consists of three main packages:

```
/d/foundry-vtt-mcp/
├── packages/
│   ├── mcp-server/          # Backend MCP server (runs in Claude Desktop)
│   │   ├── src/
│   │   │   ├── backend.ts   # MCP server entry point
│   │   │   ├── foundry-client.ts  # WebSocket client to Foundry
│   │   │   └── tools/       # 48+ MCP tool definitions
│   │   └── dist/            # Compiled JavaScript
│   │
│   ├── foundry-module/      # Foundry VTT module (runs in Foundry browser)
│   │   ├── src/
│   │   │   ├── main.ts      # Module entry point
│   │   │   ├── queries.ts   # Query handler implementations
│   │   │   └── data-access.ts  # Foundry API wrappers
│   │   ├── dist/            # Compiled JavaScript
│   │   ├── lang/            # Localization files
│   │   ├── styles/          # CSS
│   │   ├── templates/       # Handlebars templates
│   │   └── module.json      # Foundry manifest
│   │
│   └── shared/              # Shared TypeScript types
│       └── src/types.ts     # Common interfaces
│
├── scripts/
│   └── deploy-foundry.js    # Auto-deployment to Foundry modules
│
├── test/
│   ├── mcp.test (1).md      # Complete test suite (5184 lines)
│   └── test_result.md       # Live test results
│
├── foundry_docs_md/         # Foundry v13 API docs (~1659 files)
├── warhammer_system/        # WFRP 4e system code reference
│   ├── wfrp_system.js       # System mechanics (6.4MB)
│   └── wfrp.js              # Module code (1.8MB)
│
└── docs/
    ├── INSTRUCTIONS.md      # Development workflow
    └── WFRP4E_SYSTEM_GUIDE.md  # Game mechanics guide
```

### Data Flow

```
┌─────────────────┐         WebSocket (31415)        ┌──────────────────┐
│  Claude Desktop │ ◄────────────────────────────► │  Foundry VTT     │
│                 │                                  │  (Browser)       │
│  MCP Server     │         Query/Response           │                  │
│  (Node.js)      │ ◄────────────────────────────► │  Foundry Module  │
│                 │                                  │  (JavaScript)    │
└─────────────────┘                                  └──────────────────┘
       │                                                       │
       │ Calls MCP Tools                                      │ Accesses
       ▼                                                       ▼
  Tool Handlers                                      Foundry API (game.actors, etc.)
       │                                                       │
       │ Sends Query                                          │ Updates
       ▼                                                       ▼
  foundry-client.ts                                   Actor Documents
       │                                                       │
       └───────────────► queryFoundry() ──────────────────────┘
```

### Communication Protocol

1. **Claude Desktop** → User asks question about WFRP character
2. **MCP Server** → Receives tool call, executes handler
3. **Handler** → Calls `queryFoundry(queryType, data)`
4. **foundry-client.ts** → Sends query via WebSocket to Foundry
5. **Foundry Module** → Receives query in `main.ts`, routes to `queries.ts`
6. **queries.ts** → Executes handler, calls `data-access.ts` functions
7. **data-access.ts** → Calls Foundry API (`actor.update()`, etc.)
8. **Foundry API** → Updates game data, returns result
9. **Response** → Travels back through chain to Claude Desktop

### Key Files and Responsibilities

| File | Lines | Purpose |
|------|-------|---------|
| `packages/mcp-server/src/backend.ts` | 1500+ | MCP server entry, tool registration |
| `packages/mcp-server/src/tools/*.ts` | 50-200 each | Individual tool definitions (48+ tools) |
| `packages/foundry-module/src/main.ts` | 200+ | WebSocket server, query routing |
| `packages/foundry-module/src/queries.ts` | 3930+ | Query handler implementations |
| `packages/foundry-module/src/data-access.ts` | 3900+ | Foundry API wrappers |
| `shared/src/types.ts` | 500+ | Shared TypeScript interfaces |

