## 🛠️ Foundry VTT v13 API Critical Methods

### Updating Actor Data

**Direct property updates**:
```javascript
// CORRECT for Foundry v13
await actor.update({
  "system.characteristics.s.initial": 40
});

// Updates multiple fields
await actor.update({
  "system.characteristics.s.initial": 40,
  "system.status.wounds.value": 15,
  "system.status.fortune.value": 3
});
```

**DON'T use direct assignment**:
```javascript
// WRONG - doesn't persist
actor.system.characteristics.s.initial = 40;
```

### Embedded Documents (Items on Actors)

**Creating embedded documents**:
```javascript
// Add item to actor
await actor.createEmbeddedDocuments("Item", [itemData]);

// Add multiple items
await actor.createEmbeddedDocuments("Item", [item1Data, item2Data]);
```

**Updating embedded documents**:
```javascript
// Find the item first
const skill = actor.items.find(i => i.name === "Melee (Basic)");

// Update it
await skill.update({
  "system.advances.value": 10
});

// Or update via actor
await actor.updateEmbeddedDocuments("Item", [{
  _id: skill.id,
  "system.advances.value": 10
}]);
```

**Deleting embedded documents**:
```javascript
await actor.deleteEmbeddedDocuments("Item", [itemId]);
```

### Compendium Operations

**Search compendium**:
```javascript
const pack = game.packs.get("wfrp4e-core.items");
const index = await pack.getIndex();

// Search by name
const results = index.filter(i => i.name.includes("Melee"));
```

**Get document from compendium**:
```javascript
const pack = game.packs.get("wfrp4e-core.items");
const document = await pack.getDocument(itemId);
```

**Add compendium item to actor**:
```javascript
// Construct UUID
const uuid = `Compendium.${packName}.${itemId}`;

// Get document
const doc = await fromUuid(uuid);

// Add to actor
await actor.createEmbeddedDocuments("Item", [doc.toObject()]);
```

**CRITICAL**: Search results return `{pack, id}` not `{uuid}`. Always construct UUID manually:
```javascript
const uuid = `Compendium.${result.pack}.${result.id || result._id}`;
```

---

## ⚠️ Common Pitfalls & Solutions

### Issue: Updates Don't Persist

**Symptom**: Changes appear in code but not in Foundry UI
**Cause**: Using direct assignment instead of `update()`
**Fix**:
```javascript
// WRONG
actor.system.characteristics.s.initial = 40;

// CORRECT
await actor.update({"system.characteristics.s.initial": 40});
```

### Issue: Embedded Document Not Found

**Symptom**: "Item not found" errors
**Cause**: Trying to update items without finding them first
**Fix**:
```javascript
// Find the item
const item = actor.items.find(i => i.name === "Melee (Basic)");
if (!item) {
  throw new Error("Skill not found");
}

// Update it
await item.update({"system.advances.value": 10});
```

### Issue: UUID Construction Fails

**Symptom**: "Cannot add item from compendium"
**Cause**: Assuming `searchResult.uuid` exists (it doesn't)
**Fix**:
```javascript
// WRONG
const uuid = searchResult.uuid; // undefined!

// CORRECT
const uuid = `Compendium.${searchResult.pack}.${searchResult.id}`;
```

### Issue: XP Costs Wrong

**Symptom**: Charging too much/too little XP
**Cause**: Using wrong tier calculation
**Fix**:
```javascript
// CORRECT tiered formula
const tier = Math.floor(currentAdvances / 5);
const TIER_COSTS = [10, 15, 20, 30, 40, 50, 70, 90, 110, 130];
const xpCost = TIER_COSTS[tier];

// Example: 11th advance = tier 2 = 20 XP
// Math.floor(10 / 5) = 2, TIER_COSTS[2] = 20
```

### Issue: Characteristics Not Updating Properly

**Symptom**: Updating advances instead of initial value
**Cause**: Wrong data path
**Fix**:
```javascript
// For DIRECT SET (foundry-update-character-info)
await actor.update({"system.characteristics.s.initial": 40});

// For XP ADVANCE (advance-characteristic)
const char = actor.system.characteristics.s;
await actor.update({
  "system.characteristics.s.advances": char.advances + 1,
  "system.details.experience.current": xp - cost
});
```

### Issue: Career Not Detected as Current

**Symptom**: "No current career found"
**Cause**: Career item `system.current.value` not true
**Fix**:
```javascript
const currentCareer = actor.items.find(i =>
  i.type === 'career' &&
  i.system.current.value === true
);

if (!currentCareer) {
  throw new Error("No current career marked");
}
```

### Issue: Dialog Timeouts on Actor Updates (CRITICAL FOR WFRP4e)

**Symptom**: `Error: Query timeout: warhammer-mcp.updateActor` when advancing characteristics
**Cause**: WFRP4e system shows confirmation dialog: "Do you wish to proceed?" which blocks update
**Root Cause**: Missing `{ skipDialog: true }` option in `actor.update()` calls
**Fix**:
```javascript
// WRONG - causes timeout
await actor.update(updateData);

// CORRECT - bypasses WFRP4e confirmation dialogs
await actor.update(updateData, { skipDialog: true });
```

**Location**: `/d/foundry-vtt-mcp/packages/foundry-module/src/data-access.ts` line 3812

**Why This Matters**: WFRP4e adds custom dialogs for characteristic/skill advances. Without `skipDialog`, the MCP query waits forever for user to click "OK" in Foundry, causing timeouts.

### Issue: Condition Counts Not Showing

**Symptom**: Character has 3 Fatigued conditions but only shows "Fatigued" without count
**Cause**: Effect flags not being passed from data-access.ts to character.ts
**Root Cause**: Missing `flags` in effects mapping
**Fix**:
```javascript
// In data-access.ts effects mapping (line 844-856)
effects: Array.from(actor.effects || []).map((effect: any) => ({
  id: effect.id,
  name: effect.name || effect.label || 'Unknown Effect',
  ...(effect.icon ? { icon: effect.icon } : {}),
  disabled: effect.disabled,
  ...(effect.duration ? {
    duration: {
      type: (effect as any).duration.type || 'none',
      duration: (effect as any).duration.duration,
      remaining: (effect as any).duration.remaining,
    }
  } : {}),
  ...(effect.flags ? { flags: effect.flags } : {}),  // CRITICAL: Added
})),
```

**Why This Matters**: WFRP4e stores condition counts in `effect.flags.wfrp4e.conditionValue`. Without passing flags, character.ts can't format as "Fatigued (3)".

