## 🛠️ Tool Implementation Patterns

### Adding a New MCP Tool

**Step 1: Create Tool File** (`packages/mcp-server/src/tools/your-tool.ts`)
```typescript
import { Tool } from '@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/types.js';
import { queryFoundry } from '../foundry-client.js';

export const yourToolDefinition: Tool = {
  name: 'warhammer-mcp__your-tool-name',
  description: 'Clear description of what this tool does',
  inputSchema: {
    type: 'object',
    properties: {
      characterName: {
        type: 'string',
        description: 'Name of the character'
      },
      value: {
        type: 'number',
        description: 'Value to set'
      }
    },
    required: ['characterName']
  }
};

export async function handleYourTool(args: {
  characterName: string;
  value?: number;
}) {
  const result = await queryFoundry('foundry-mcp-bridge.yourHandler', {
    characterName: args.characterName,
    value: args.value
  });

  return {
    content: [{
      type: 'text',
      text: JSON.stringify(result, null, 2)
    }]
  };
}
```

**Step 2: Register Tool** (`packages/mcp-server/src/backend.ts`)
```typescript
// Import the tool
import { yourToolDefinition, handleYourTool } from './tools/your-tool.js';

// Add to tools list (around line 100)
server.setRequestHandler(ListToolsRequestSchema, async () => ({
  tools: [
    // ... existing tools
    yourToolDefinition,
  ]
}));

// Add handler (around line 1300-1450)
server.setRequestHandler(CallToolRequestSchema, async (request) => {
  const { name, arguments: args } = request.params;

  switch (name) {
    // ... existing cases

    case 'warhammer-mcp__your-tool-name':
      return await handleYourTool(args);

    // ... rest of cases
  }
});
```

**Step 3: Add Foundry Handler** (`packages/foundry-module/src/queries.ts`)
```typescript
// Add case in handleQuery function (line ~100-3900)
case 'foundry-mcp-bridge.yourHandler': {
  const { characterName, value } = data;

  // Get actor
  const actor = await dataAccess.getActorByName(characterName);
  if (!actor) {
    return {
      success: false,
      error: `Character "${characterName}" not found`
    };
  }

  // Perform update (ALWAYS use skipDialog for WFRP4e)
  await actor.update({
    "system.your.path": value
  }, { skipDialog: true });

  return {
    success: true,
    message: `Updated ${characterName}`
  };
}
```

### XP Tiered Cost Formula (CRITICAL)

WFRP 4e uses tiered XP costs for advances:
```typescript
const TIER_COSTS = [10, 15, 20, 30, 40, 50, 70, 90, 110, 130];

// Calculate tier based on current advances
const tier = Math.floor(currentAdvances / 5);
const xpCost = TIER_COSTS[Math.min(tier, TIER_COSTS.length - 1)];

// Examples:
// Advance 1-5:   tier 0 = 10 XP each
// Advance 6-10:  tier 1 = 15 XP each
// Advance 11-15: tier 2 = 20 XP each
// Advance 50+:   tier 9 = 130 XP each
```

### Compendium UUID Construction (CRITICAL)

**Search results DO NOT include UUID** - you must construct it manually:
```typescript
// WRONG - searchResult.uuid doesn't exist!
const uuid = searchResult.uuid;

// CORRECT - construct manually
const uuid = `Compendium.${searchResult.pack}.${searchResult.id || searchResult._id}`;

// Example:
const packName = "wfrp4e-core.skills";
const itemId = "abc123";
const uuid = `Compendium.wfrp4e-core.skills.abc123`;

// Then get document
const doc = await fromUuid(uuid);
```

### Validation and Capping

**Always validate and cap values**:
```typescript
// Cap characteristics (reasonable max: 100, warn if >250)
if (value > 250) {
  return {
    success: false,
    error: `Value ${value} is unreasonably high (max recommended: 100)`
  };
}

// Cap Fortune to Fate maximum
const fateMax = actor.system.status.fate.max;
const fortuneValue = Math.min(value, fateMax);

if (value > fateMax) {
  // Still apply capped value but warn user
  await actor.update({
    "system.status.fortune.value": fortuneValue
  }, { skipDialog: true });

  return {
    success: true,
    warning: `Fortune capped at Fate maximum (${fateMax})`,
    value: fortuneValue
  };
}
```

